Subject: [PATCH] atmel_mxt: keep the input device across a configuration update

Some 16 s after every start the driver writes its configuration file into the
touch controller again (mxt_update_firmware_cfg -> mxt_self_update_cfg), even when
the controller already has it: ASUS commented out the early return for a matching
CRC. Before writing, it unregistered the touchscreen's input device, and afterwards
it registered a new one. Android copes with a device going away and coming back;
TWRP logs "Reloading input devices" and from then on ignores the touch, although
the touches reach the kernel (getevent sees them on the new node).

The input device now stays: mxt_self_update_cfg no longer frees it, and
mxt_configure_objects makes one only when there is none, as at probe and after the
explicit update paths (mxt_load_cfg, mxt_load_fw), which still free it first. The
configuration file is the same at every start, so the axes the device was set up
with at probe do not change.
---
--- drivers/input/touchscreen/atmel_z500/atmel_mxt_ts_1666t2.c
+++ drivers/input/touchscreen/atmel_z500/atmel_mxt_ts_1666t2.c
@@ -3972,7 +3972,9 @@
 			LDBG("error2 %d updating config\n", error2);
 	}
 
-	if (data->T9_reportid_min) {
+	if (data->input_dev) {
+		/* kept across a configuration update, see mxt_self_update_cfg() */
+	} else if (data->T9_reportid_min) {
 		error = mxt_initialize_t9_input_device(data);
 		if (error)
 			goto err_free_object_table;
@@ -4584,8 +4586,12 @@
 		goto out;
 	}
 	data->updating_config = true;
-	
-	mxt_free_input_device(data);
+
+	/*
+	 * The input device stays: mxt_configure_objects() leaves an existing one
+	 * alone. A new one registered every boot, some 16 s in, and from then on
+	 * TWRP ignored the touch, although the touches reached the new device.
+	 */
 
 	if (data->suspended) {
 		if (data->use_regulator) {
